# Captain never reads logs (agent does)

## Hard gate — zero exceptions

The **user / captain never** opens, reads, pastes, or checks:
- game logs
- mod logs
- error dumps
- JSON/data files
- build reports
- transcripts
- any text file on disk

**That is always the agent's job.** Read from disk with Read / Grep / Shell. If a path is wrong, search the disk. Report findings in plain English.

**Never ask the captain to do file/log work. Ever.**

## Forbidden (never say or imply)

- "Paste the log"
- "Open quest_tracker_log and tell me…"
- "Check re2_framework_log for errors"
- "Send me the output of…"
- "Can you look at the log and see if…"
- "After you play, read the log and confirm…"
- Putting log-reading on any user/captain todo list

## Captain's job (only these)

- Install mods via Fluffy when asked
- Play the game
- Say what they saw (PASS/FAIL, what felt wrong)
- Screenshots when something looks wrong on screen
- Yes/no on code or config changes

## Agent paths (DD2)

- Game: `C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Dragons Dogma 2\re2_framework_log.txt`
- Quest Tracker: `...\reframework\data\quest_tracker_log.txt`
- Other mods: `reframework\data\*_log.txt`
- Workspace: `tools\`, `_BACKUP_TOUCHES\`, agent transcripts

